    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter August 25th with a primary objective of capitalizing on speed-dependent matchups. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) is our premier play of the day; the combination of a favorable matchup against Brandon Pfaadt and a projected leadoff spot provides elite upside, particularly given his sprint speed and the high probability of a green light against a pitcher with a slow delivery. Following him, **Junior Caminero** (74.78) and **Yordan Alvarez** (73.61) anchor our middle order. **Yordan Alvarez** continues to operate as an offensive engine due to his elite 0.458 xwOBA, while **Junior Caminero** finds himself in a high-leverage spot against Jobe, benefiting from a significant park and platoon boost that pushes his efficiency rating well into the \"Strong\" tier.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Carson Benge** (36.49), who fell just shy of our 40-point floor. While his base projection remained respectable, the combination of a stiff matchup against Harrison and a disadvantageous L/L platoon alignment forced the optimizer to bench him in favor of higher-ceiling options. Meanwhile, we are monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, and **Lars Nootbaar**. While **Trea Turner** remains a mandatory start despite facing the high-caliber George Kirby, his score is bolstered by his anticipated #2 spot in the order. We are maintaining caution regarding **Dillon Dingler** (44.07); despite his inclusion, his dynamic platoon penalty against Legumina makes him a marginal start, and he remains the most likely candidate to be subbed out should late-breaking news emerge regarding his position in the order.",
